{
  "comment": [
    "Benchmark fixture manifest (FABLE_SOLVER_OPTIMIZATION_REPORT §12 / PR-1).",
    "Run via: node scripts/bench-matrix.mjs [--exe <path>] [--runs 5] [--only <name,...>]",
    "Every fixture is a full CLI solve (NOT --benchmark presets) so the JSON",
    "carries resources.measured_* and tree_mode provenance.",
    "Contract (GPT Phase-0 review P1-3/P1-5): every fixture DECLARES",
    "expected_tree_mode and (if capped) expected_threads; the harness",
    "hard-fails the fixture when the solve's tree_mode differs or the",
    "effective thread count is silently clamped below the request — a",
    "collapsed run must never be quoted as an enumerated baseline, and an",
    "8-thread run must never be quoted as 16T.",
    "Correctness micros live in ctest (smoke|parity labels), not here.",
    "T0/0b: the `accuracy` family measures TIME TO TARGET, not iterations/sec.",
    "Iterations/sec is not comparable across engines and not what a solver is",
    "bought for; PioSOLVER's own benchmarks quote time to 0.5/0.3/0.1/0.05%",
    "of pot. One solve to the tightest target yields every looser threshold",
    "off the recorded convergence curve.",
    "T0/0c: the `target` family is the 4.65M-node memory unlock (ROADMAP §1,",
    "'the one number that matters'). Reproduced from the app's own data:",
    "m0 = MATCHUPS[0] UTG vs MP SRP (pot 5.5bb, stack 97.5bb -> chip units",
    "x10, SPR 17.7), b6/b7 = BOARD_TEMPLATES[6]/[7] monotone, standard menus",
    "= flop/turn/river 0.33,0.75 (the CLI default turn/river is a SINGLE size,",
    "which is why these need explicit flags).",
    "mono_full_menu_estimate is the METER: it forces the enumerated tree with",
    "a huge host budget and records what the GPU state would cost. That number",
    "(measured 2026-07-27: 31,683 MB device total) is what B3 has to drive",
    "under the ~24,211 MB VRAM budget. It is green today and stays green — the",
    "number it carries is the progress signal, not its pass/fail.",
    "mono_full_menu_gpu is the GATE: the same spot actually routed to CUDA. It",
    "carries known_gap so it reports red without failing the run — being red",
    "today is the point (ROADMAP §5 rule 2), and it turns green when B3 lands."
  ],
